Theorem CH-108: interprocedural_summary engine bootstrap (IC-3 ParamContract join on 2-call-site graph)

  Preconditions:
    - G is a synthetic 2-call-site graph per Annex E §AIMS
      IC-2 + IC-3 with one callee g and two caller call sites
      site_1 and site_2 both calling g
    - the AimsState dimension under analysis is Access x Consumption
      per Annex E §AIMS §3.1 + §AIMS §3.2
    - site_1 passes argument state (Borrowed, Linear) to g
    - site_2 passes argument state (Owned, Affine) to g
    - IC-3 ParamContract join per Annex E §AIMS: callee's
      parameter contract is the componentwise max of all
      call-site argument states
    - interprocedural_summary engine consumes SCC topological order
      witness, per-node finite enumeration over contract dimensions,
      and constructive contract-join derivation per the foundational-axiom policy
      sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape

  Soundness property:
    Forall G in synthetic 2-call-site graphs over the
    Access x Consumption sub-lattice.
      ParamContract(g) is equal to the componentwise max of all
        call-site argument states;
      i.e. ParamContract(g) is the join of site_1's argument and
        site_2's argument per IC-3.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive contract-join derivation with per-call-site finite
    enumeration.

      Setup:
        site_1.arg = (Borrowed, Linear);
        site_2.arg = (Owned, Affine);
        ParamContract(g) is computed by IC-3 join over the
        call-site argument set { site_1.arg, site_2.arg }.

      Componentwise join derivation:
        Access dimension: max(Borrowed, Owned) = Owned
          (per L-1 + L-4: Borrowed less-than Owned; max yields
           the upper element).
        Consumption dimension: max(Linear, Affine) = Affine
          (per L-1 + L-4: Linear less-than Affine; max yields
           the upper element).
        Therefore ParamContract(g) = (Owned, Affine).

      Witness exhibition:
        The IC-3 join is exhibited as the explicit max-pair
        (Owned, Affine); no LEM or choice axiom required; the
        finite-domain join is constructively computed per the
        case_analysis sub-discharge.

      Closed-world coverage:
        The call-site set is exactly { site_1, site_2 }; the
        per-call-site enumeration covers both sites; the join is
        idempotent on the empty case (no call sites means
        ParamContract is the most-optimistic initial value per
        IC-2) and monotone on the per-site addition.

    SCC topological-order witness:
      G has one SCC for g (size 1) and one SCC each for site_1's
      and site_2's enclosing functions (the callers); topological
      order processes g after its callees (g has no callees in
      this synthetic graph; topological order is g first under
      the standard "process callees before callers" interpretation,
      but for IC-3 join purposes the order is "callee's contract
      reads caller's call-site arguments"; both interpretations
      yield the same converged contract in this 2-call-site
      bootstrap case).

    Lattice validation:
      L-1 (commutativity of join) ensures the join is independent
      of which call-site argument is processed first. L-4
      (partial-order reflexivity, antisymmetry, transitivity)
      ensures the join is well-defined on the sub-lattice. L-6
      (monotonicity) ensures the join is monotone over the
      per-call-site lattice product.

    Contract-soundness claim:
      The derived ParamContract (Owned, Affine) is the LUB of the
      call-site argument set per IC-3; therefore it
      conservatively over-approximates every call site's argument;
      it is sound for downstream consumption per the IC-3
      contract.

    Engines dispatched:
      interprocedural_summary (SCC topological-order witness;
                               per-call-site finite enumeration;
                               constructive contract-join
                               derivation)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: 01A bootstrap discharged via §01A Implementation Items (engine constructive verification + Lean 4 cross-validation)
